# EnergySense requires NO environment variables.
#
# Verified against the codebase: there is no os.environ / os.getenv / dotenv
# usage in app.py, model.py, data_gen.py, tariffs.py or agent.py. The app runs
# fully offline with hard-coded local paths:
#
#   data/smart_meter.csv   synthetic dataset (regenerated when missing)
#   data/model.pkl         trained RandomForest (retrained when missing)
#   data/metrics.json      hold-out metrics (rewritten when retrained)
#   http://127.0.0.1:5000  bind address/port fixed in app.py (__main__ block)
#
# A real .env is ignored by Git. If you add configuration of your own, this is
# the place to document it; nothing below is read by the application.
#
# Example of the format, for future additions only:
#   SOME_FUTURE_SETTING=placeholder-value
